Ven, Espíritu Santo
  Archidiócesis de Toledo (Spain), "Cadena de oración por la asamblea del
  Sínodo", 2026, section "Invocación al Espíritu Santo".
  Copied from https://www.architoledo.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Cadena-de-oracion.pdf
  The PDF carries no copyright notice. Traditional prayer (the Latin "Veni,
  Sancte Spiritus, reple tuorum corda fidelium" with the Pentecost collect);
  the Spanish wording is the archdiocese's.

Ven, Espíritu Creador (Veni Creator)
  Holy See, "Compendio del Catecismo de la Iglesia Católica" (2005),
  Apéndice A, "Oraciones comunes".
  Copied from https://www.vatican.va/archive/compendium_ccc/documents/archive_2005_compendium-ccc_sp.html
  The same text is on https://www.vaticannews.va/es/oraciones/veni-creator.html
  © Copyright 2005 - Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  The Latin hymn (9th century) is in the public domain.

Secuencia de Pentecostés
  Holy See, "Compendio del Catecismo de la Iglesia Católica" (2005),
  Apéndice A, "Ven Santo Espíritu"; the same text as the Spanish Lectionary
  (Conferencia Episcopal Española, Leccionario I (C), Domingo de Pentecostés).
  Copied from https://www.vatican.va/archive/compendium_ccc/documents/archive_2005_compendium-ccc_sp.html
  The same text is on https://www.vaticannews.va/es/oraciones/ven-santo-espiritu.html
  and https://www.conferenciaepiscopal.es/liturgia/cpentecostes.pdf
  © Copyright 2005 - Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  The Lectionary PDF carries no notice. The Latin sequence (about 1200) is in
  the public domain.
  Ends at "y danos tu gozo eterno." with no "Amén", as in the Lectionary.

Salmo 23, Salmo 27 and Salmo 51
  "La Biblia. El Libro del Pueblo de Dios" (traducción argentina), as the
  Holy See's site publishes it:
    Salmo 23  https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PGS.HTM
    Salmo 27  https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PGW.HTM
    Salmo 51  https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PHK.HTM
  Copyright © Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  Used with attribution; all rights remain with the publisher.
  The psalms follow the source's Hebrew numbering. Their superscriptions and
  the verse numbers are left out.

Magníficat (Lucas 1, 46-55)
  "La Biblia. El Libro del Pueblo de Dios" (traducción argentina), as the
  Holy See's site publishes it.
  Copied from https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PVJ.HTM
  Copyright © Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  Used with attribution; all rights remain with the publisher.
  The text starts at «Mi alma canta» (the narrative "María dijo entonces:" is
  left out) and the verse numbers are left out. Two transcription typos of
  the page are corrected, as the Bible reads:
    Lc 1, 48  "porque el miró" is given as "porque él miró"
    Lc 1, 49  "el Todopoderoso he hecho" is given as "el Todopoderoso ha hecho"

